    <item>
      <title>[翻译] Simon Willison: 从零开始的量化技术</title>
      <link>https://simonwillison.net/2026/Mar/26/quantization-from-the-ground-up/#atom-everything</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;标签:&lt;/strong&gt; #量化 #LLM #模型压缩&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;摘要:&lt;/strong&gt; 本文深入浅出地讲解了AI模型量化技术，不仅提供了浮点数二进制表示的可视化解析，还重点探讨了“异常值”（超级权重）对模型质量的关键影响——删除单个即可能导致模型输出乱码，并通过测试证实16位到8位量化几乎无损，4位量化仍能保持约90%的原始性能。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="color:#888;font-size:13px;"&gt;原标题: Quantization from the ground up&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr/&gt;
&lt;h3 style="margin:24px 0 12px;"&gt;Quantization from the ground up&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;div style="color:#9a9ea6;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;margin:20px 0 6px;"&gt;
Also included is the best visual explanation I've ever seen of how floating point numbers are represented using binary digits.
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p style="color:#2c2c2e;margin:4px 0 24px;line-height:1.8;font-size:15px;"&gt;
文中还包含了我见过的关于&lt;strong style="color:#c0392b;background:#fdf2f2;padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;"&gt;浮点数（floating point numbers）&lt;/strong&gt;如何使用&lt;strong style="color:#c0392b;background:#fdf2f2;padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;"&gt;二进制数字（binary digits）&lt;/strong&gt;表示的最佳可视化解释。
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;img src="https://static.simonwillison.net/static/2026/float.jpg" alt="Screenshot of an interactive float32 binary representation tool showing the value -48.92364502, with color-coded bit fields labeled S (sign), EXPONENT (blue), and SIGNIFICAND (pink), displaying the 32-bit pattern 11000010010000111101100001110100000, and a slider control at the bottom along with minus, plus, and reset buttons." style="max-width:100%;border-radius:8px;margin:12px 0;"/&gt;

&lt;img src="https://static.simonwillison.net/static/2026/float.jpg" alt="Screenshot of an interactive float32 binary representation tool showing the value -48.92364502, with color-coded bit fields labeled S (sign), EXPONENT (blue), and SIGNIFICAND (pink), displaying the 32-bit pattern 11000010010000111101100001110100000, and a slider control at the bottom along with minus, plus, and reset buttons." style="max-width:100%;border-radius:8px;margin:12px 0;"/&gt;

&lt;div style="color:#9a9ea6;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;margin:20px 0 6px;"&gt;
I hadn't heard about outlier values in quantization - rare float values that exist outside of the normal tiny-value distribution - but apparently they're very important:
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p style="color:#2c2c2e;margin:4px 0 24px;line-height:1.8;font-size:15px;"&gt;
我从未听说过量化中的&lt;strong style="color:#c0392b;background:#fdf2f2;padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;"&gt;异常值（outlier values）&lt;/strong&gt;——那些存在于正常微小值分布之外的罕见浮点数值——但显然它们非常重要：
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div style="color:#9a9ea6;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;margin:20px 0 6px;"&gt;
&lt;blockquote style="border-left:3px solid #c0c0c0;padding:8px 16px;margin:8px 0;background:#f9f9fb;"&gt;
Why do these outliers exist? [...] tl;dr: no one conclusively knows, but a small fraction of these outliers are very important to model quality. Removing even a single "super weight," as Apple calls them, can cause the model to output complete gibberish.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p style="color:#2c2c2e;margin:4px 0 24px;line-height:1.8;font-size:15px;"&gt;
&lt;blockquote style="border-left:3px solid #c0c0c0;padding:8px 16px;margin:8px 0;background:#f9f9fb;"&gt;
为什么这些异常值会存在？[...] 简而言之：没有人确切知道，但这些异常值中的一小部分对模型质量&lt;strong style="color:#c0392b;background:#fdf2f2;padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;"&gt;非常&lt;/strong&gt;重要。正如&lt;strong style="color:#2471a3;background:#eaf4fd;padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;"&gt;Apple（苹果）&lt;/strong&gt;所称，即使移除单个"&lt;strong style="color:#c0392b;background:#fdf2f2;padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;"&gt;超级权重（super weight）&lt;/strong&gt;"，也可能导致模型输出完全混乱的内容。
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div style="color:#9a9ea6;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;margin:20px 0 6px;"&gt;
Given their importance, real-world quantization schemes sometimes do extra work to preserve these outliers. They might do this by not quantizing them at all, or by saving their location and value into a separate table, then removing them so that their block isn't destroyed.
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p style="color:#2c2c2e;margin:4px 0 24px;line-height:1.8;font-size:15px;"&gt;
鉴于它们的重要性，实际的&lt;strong style="color:#c0392b;background:#fdf2f2;padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;"&gt;量化方案（quantization schemes）&lt;/strong&gt;有时会做额外的工作来保留这些异常值。它们可能会通过完全不对这些值进行量化来实现这一点，或者将它们的的位置和值保存到一个单独的表中，然后将其移除，以免破坏它们所在的块。
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div style="color:#9a9ea6;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;margin:20px 0 6px;"&gt;
Why do these outliers exist? [...] tl;dr: no one conclusively knows, but a small fraction of these outliers are very important to model quality. Removing even a single "super weight," as Apple calls them, can cause the model to output complete gibberish.
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p style="color:#2c2c2e;margin:4px 0 24px;line-height:1.8;font-size:15px;"&gt;
为什么这些异常值会存在？[...] 简而言之：没有人确切知道，但这些异常值中的一小部分对模型质量非常重要。正如&lt;strong style="color:#2471a3;background:#eaf4fd;padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;"&gt;Apple（苹果）&lt;/strong&gt;所称，即使移除单个"&lt;strong style="color:#c0392b;background:#fdf2f2;padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;"&gt;超级权重（super weight）&lt;/strong&gt;"，也可能导致模型输出完全混乱的内容。
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div style="color:#9a9ea6;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;margin:20px 0 6px;"&gt;
Given their importance, real-world quantization schemes sometimes do extra work to preserve these outliers. They might do this by not quantizing them at all, or by saving their location and value into a separate table, then removing them so that their block isn't destroyed.
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p style="color:#2c2c2e;margin:4px 0 24px;line-height:1.8;font-size:15px;"&gt;
鉴于它们的重要性，实际的&lt;strong style="color:#c0392b;background:#fdf2f2;padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;"&gt;量化方案（quantization schemes）&lt;/strong&gt;有时会做额外的工作来保留这些异常值。它们可能会通过完全不对这些值进行量化来实现这一点，或者将它们的的位置和值保存到一个单独的表中，然后将其移除，以免破坏它们所在的块。
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div style="color:#9a9ea6;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;margin:20px 0 6px;"&gt;
Plus there's a section on How much does quantization affect model accuracy?. Sam explains the concepts of perplexity and &lt;strong&gt;KL divergence&lt;/strong&gt; and then uses the llama.cpp perplexity tool and a run of the GPQA benchmark to show how different quantization levels affect Qwen 3.5 9B.
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p style="color:#2c2c2e;margin:4px 0 24px;line-height:1.8;font-size:15px;"&gt;
此外，文章还有一个关于"&lt;strong style="color:#c0392b;background:#fdf2f2;padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;"&gt;量化对模型精度的影响有多大（How much does quantization affect model accuracy?）&lt;/strong&gt;"的章节。&lt;strong style="color:#2471a3;background:#eaf4fd;padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;"&gt;Sam（山姆）&lt;/strong&gt;解释了&lt;strong style="color:#c0392b;background:#fdf2f2;padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;"&gt;困惑度（perplexity）&lt;/strong&gt;和&lt;strong style="color:#c0392b;background:#fdf2f2;padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;"&gt;KL 散度（KL divergence）&lt;/strong&gt;的概念，然后使用&lt;strong style="color:#2471a3;background:#eaf4fd;padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;"&gt;llama.cpp&lt;/strong&gt;的困惑度工具和运行&lt;strong style="color:#c0392b;background:#fdf2f2;padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;"&gt;GPQA 基准测试（GPQA benchmark）&lt;/strong&gt;来展示不同的量化级别如何影响&lt;strong style="color:#2471a3;background:#eaf4fd;padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;"&gt;Qwen 3.5 9B&lt;/strong&gt;。
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div style="color:#9a9ea6;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;margin:20px 0 6px;"&gt;
His conclusion:
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p style="color:#2c2c2e;margin:4px 0 24px;line-height:1.8;font-size:15px;"&gt;
他的结论是：
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div style="color:#9a9ea6;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;margin:20px 0 6px;"&gt;
&lt;blockquote style="border-left:3px solid #c0c0c0;padding:8px 16px;margin:8px 0;background:#f9f9fb;"&gt;
It looks like 16-bit to 8-bit carries almost no quality penalty. 16-bit to 4-bit is more noticeable, but it's certainly not a quarter as good as the original. Closer to 90%, depending on how you want to measure it.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p style="color:#2c2c2e;margin:4px 0 24px;line-height:1.8;font-size:15px;"&gt;
&lt;blockquote style="border-left:3px solid #c0c0c0;padding:8px 16px;margin:8px 0;background:#f9f9fb;"&gt;
看起来从 16 位到 8 位的转换几乎不会造成质量损失。16 位到 4 位的转换更为明显，但效果肯定不比原版的四分之一好。根据测量方式的不同，更接近 90%。
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div style="color:#9a9ea6;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;margin:20px 0 6px;"&gt;
It looks like 16-bit to 8-bit carries almost no quality penalty. 16-bit to 4-bit is more noticeable, but it's certainly not a quarter as good as the original. Closer to 90%, depending on how you want to measure it.
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p style="color:#2c2c2e;margin:4px 0 24px;line-height:1.8;font-size:15px;"&gt;
看起来从 16 位到 8 位的转换几乎不会造成质量损失。16 位到 4 位的转换更为明显，但效果肯定不比原版的四分之一好。根据测量方式的不同，更接近 90%。
&lt;/p&gt;

